        "answer": false,
        "explanation": "No. The limit is enforced entirely inside `basket_total` in this repository. Whatever function the caller passes in to reach io-pricing runs on a worker pool, and the page stops waiting with `future.result(timeout=0.3s)`. A call whose reported `took_ms` is over the limit is also treated as having run out of time. In both cases `PricingServiceFailed` is raised, and `account_page._the_basket_for` already catches it and renders the page without the basket total. No change is needed in io-pricing, in the caller's connection code or in configuration for the page to stop waiting 1500ms. If io-pricing slows down like this again, the account page will cap the wait at about 300ms and show \"Pricing is not available right now\" instead of the total."
